  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "cortical-neuronal-2e72",
  "summary": "Recent preprints fit neural control and field models to mouse kinematics and cortical LFPs with physics simulation and Bayesian inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is explicit optimization of computational models against measured biological data. Two preprints train neural control policies that actuate biomechanical animal models in MJX physics simulation. MIMIC-MJX reproduces real kinematic trajectories, and a musculoskeletal mouse forelimb model recapitulates kinematics through GPU-accelerated imitation learning. A third preprint applies Bayesian joint state and parameter estimation to a discretized Wilson-Cowan Amari neural field model fitted to mouse cortical local field potentials. A fourth interprets a neural foundation model of visual activity through decoding and encoding manifolds. The published network control framework estimates regional intrinsic neural timescales from connectome structure and validates them against fMRI timescales. What is new is the constraint target: these models are tested against kinematic, population-level, and spatial readouts rather than decision behavior. The set is heterogeneous in scale and modality, so the shared element is the objective rather than the system.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
}
